      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<section class=\"secret\">\n<p>As long as the coat has a creature grappled it can use its action to swing it's victim's arms, potentially striking allies. All creatures adjacent to the grappled creature must make a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 5 (1d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage on a failed save.</p>\n<p>If the victim of the coat has a melee weapon in their hands, substitute the d4 with the weapon's damage if it's higher. The victim may choose to drop their held weapon as a reaction to this before the damage is done.</p>\n</section>\n<p>The coat causes its victim to flail about violently!</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "",
          "revision": 1,
          "rules": "2014"
        },
